# CR 702.16k, 113.7a, 608.2h: protection from a player prevents the damage of sources that player controls, and a source that
# has left the battlefield is judged as it last existed there, its controller included. Bot2 controls Absolute Virtue and on
# turn 6 steals Bot1's Fanatical Firebrand with Act of Treason. Bot2 targets itself with the Firebrand (legal: Bot2 controls the
# Firebrand) and sacrifices it as the cost, so the Firebrand is in Bot1's graveyard as the ability resolves. Its last controller
# was Bot2, not an opponent of Bot2's, so the target is still legal and the 1 damage is dealt to Bot2; judged by its owner Bot1
# the target would be illegal and the damage prevented.

